WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.832
The ground was moving, and Aladdin started to run for his life!

2
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:25.051
"Stay!" shouted Magrib and he grabbed Aladdin by the collar of his new jacket.

3
00:00:25.052 --> 00:00:30.369
Then Magrib raised his hand and struck the boy across the face.

4
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:35.944
Aladdin's cap went flying, and his teeth rattled in his head.

5
00:00:35.945 --> 00:00:40.034
He fell to the ground, weeping with pain and fear.

6
00:00:40.035 --> 00:00:42.208
"Uncle!" he cried.

7
00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:43.488
"What did I do?

8
00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:46.104
Why did you strike me?"

9
00:00:46.105 --> 00:00:51.185
"I'm sorry, but I was angered by your fear," said Magrib.

10
00:00:51.186 --> 00:00:55.126
"I am your uncle, and you must always obey me.

11
00:00:55.127 --> 00:00:56.924
You must not be afraid.

12
00:00:56.925 --> 00:00:59.389
You must not run away."

13
00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:05.908
Magrib set Aladdin's cap back on his head and brushed the dust from his clothes.

14
00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:09.227
"I will try to be brave, Uncle," said Aladdin.

15
00:01:09.228 --> 00:01:12.378
"Be calm, my boy," said Magrib.

16
00:01:12.379 --> 00:01:16.086
"Come and see how my magic has opened the earth."

17
00:01:16.087 --> 00:01:19.516
"Magic?" breathed Aladdin.

18
00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:23.922
Magrib stretched out his arm and pointed with his finger.

19
00:01:23.923 --> 00:01:31.094
Where the earth had split, Aladdin saw a thick piece of marble with a big brass ring on top.

20
00:01:31.095 --> 00:01:35.446
"What is this?" Aladdin asked.

21
00:01:35.447 --> 00:01:40.216
"It is a special door," answered the magician. "Listen closely.

22
00:01:40.217 --> 00:01:45.734
Do exactly as I say and you will be mightier and richer than any king."

23
00:01:45.735 --> 00:01:47.945
"Tell me what to do!" cried Aladdin.

24
00:01:47.946 --> 00:01:50.733
"I will obey every word!"

25
00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:55.323
"Under this marble door is a treasure," said Magrib.

26
00:01:55.324 --> 00:01:57.198
"It is for you alone.

27
00:01:57.199 --> 00:02:00.182
No one but you may claim it."

28
00:02:00.183 --> 00:02:03.388
"How do I get to the treasure?" asked Aladdin.

29
00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:08.542
"Grab the brass ring and lift the stone," said the magician.

30
00:02:08.543 --> 00:02:10.699
"What?" gasped Aladdin.

31
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:13.136
He looked down at the marble.

32
00:02:13.137 --> 00:02:14.764
"Oh, Uncle," he said.

33
00:02:14.765 --> 00:02:18.065
"It is huge—it must be so heavy.

34
00:02:18.066 --> 00:02:20.491
I am not strong enough to lift it by myself.

35
00:02:20.492 --> 00:02:22.407
You must help me!"

36
00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.517
"I cannot help you," said Magrib.

37
00:02:25.518 --> 00:02:28.383
"No one but you has the power to lift it.

38
00:02:28.384 --> 00:02:31.751
No one but you may touch it!"

39
00:02:31.752 --> 00:02:34.584
"But, Uncle!" cried Aladdin.

40
00:02:34.585 --> 00:02:38.663
"Reach out your hand, grab the ring, and pull," ordered Magrib.

41
00:02:38.664 --> 00:02:42.433
"Then say your name and command the stone to rise.

42
00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:43.957
It will obey you.

43
00:02:43.958 --> 00:02:47.134
I promise it will not be heavy."

44
00:02:47.135 --> 00:02:49.069
"But how can that be?"

45
00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:52.625
"Open the door," said Magrib.

46
00:02:52.626 --> 00:02:56.449
Unsure, the boy looked down at the marble.

47
00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.074
"I cannot do it," he said to himself.

48
00:03:00.075 --> 00:03:03.953
"Open the door!" shouted Magrib.

49
00:03:03.954 --> 00:03:08.005
Aladdin repeated the command to himself softly.

50
00:03:08.006 --> 00:03:10.825
"My name is Aladdin," he said.

51
00:03:10.826 --> 00:03:13.202
"I command you to rise."

52
00:03:13.203 --> 00:03:15.713
Then he repeated it louder.

53
00:03:15.714 --> 00:03:17.383
"My name is Aladdin.

54
00:03:17.384 --> 00:03:20.471
I command you to rise."

55
00:03:20.472 --> 00:03:23.504
"Do it, boy," hissed Magrib.

56
00:03:23.505 --> 00:03:27.995
Aladdin rubbed his hands together and took a deep breath.

57
00:03:27.996 --> 00:03:33.635
He reached out his hand, grabbed the brass ring, and pulled.

58
00:03:33.636 --> 00:03:36.079
"My name is Aladdin!" he shouted.

59
00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.559
"I command you to rise!"

60
00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.351
As the boy pulled, the stone rose.

61
00:03:42.352 --> 00:03:45.312
Aladdin was amazed.

62
00:03:45.313 --> 00:03:50.490
Within moments, he had removed the door and tossed it aside!

63
00:03:50.491 --> 00:03:56.640
He now saw a deep, dark hole where the marble had been.

64
00:03:56.641 --> 00:04:00.584
Magrib leaned over and looked into the opening.

65
00:04:00.585 --> 00:04:07.152
They could both see a steep stone stairway disappearing down into the shadows.

66
00:04:07.153 --> 00:04:09.177
Aladdin looked up at Magrib.

67
00:04:09.178 --> 00:04:12.322
"Where is the treasure?" he asked.

68
00:04:12.323 --> 00:04:15.652
"It is down there," said the magician.

69
00:04:15.653 --> 00:04:17.660
"Let's go!" shouted Aladdin.

70
00:04:17.661 --> 00:04:20.325
"Let's go and get it right now!"

71
00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:25.363
"No one can enter the enchanted treasury but you," said Magrib.

72
00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:31.053
"You must go alone."
